 "open_polygons": [],
 "notes": "Lines on this map (1972 use districts, sheet 7, Noe Valley): thin lines about 2-3 px wide close each block on its own, with blank street paper between; heavy lines about 5-7 px wide are zoning district borders. Some run in the street just beside a block outline (around the top block at x 2405-2520, y 2330-2377; along x 2680-2700 down the C-2 strip; along y 3025-3040 and y 3150-3163 between and through rows; x 2199-2204 / 2213 at y 3030-3150), others step through blocks along lot lines. A block outline is told from a border by width (the border about twice as heavy) and because it closes one rectangle, while a border carries on across streets and blocks. Corners sit on the outer edge of each block's thin line, read off the 4x ruled close-ups and confirmed with ink-run printouts along rows and columns near each corner. Box chosen at x 1810-2749 to keep out the Blanche/Nellie/Severn/Quane alleys east of x 2757, where heavy borders lie over dead-end alleys and it is unclear whether the alley splits the block. Judgment calls: (1) blocks crossed by heavy borders are typed whole, as no thin line shows under the border: column x 2640-2732 (borders at x 2682-2700 through every row), x 2537-2625 y 2861-3071 (border at y 2901-2906 and y 3025-3038), x 2323-2514 and x 2539-2732 at y 3155-3163, x 2425-2512 y 2887-2892, x 2213-2298 y 3026-3031. (2) In the bottom row the blocks x 2323-2515 and x 2539-2733 span what would be the Clipper and Jersey street lines: no line is printed across them, so each is one block. (3) The right edge shows the left line of blocks beyond the box at x 2747-2751, y 2330-2358 and x 2748-2751, y 2388-2593: typed as slivers; the lower sliver's bottom is hidden by the TWENTY-FOURTH lettering from y 2544 and was set from the row's other bottoms (about 2593). Rows below show no such line inside the box. (4) Lettering touching block lines (C-2 at x 2730-2750, y 2760-2850; TWENTY-FOURTH at x 2726-2750; R-3, R-2, R-4 and street names) is ignored; corners follow the thin lines; the right sides of x 2640-2730 blocks at y 2580-2594 and 2800-2833 were set from the line above the touching letters. (5) Top row cut by the box at y 2330 (about 30 px of each block shown) is typed. (6) A heavy line at y 2326-2332 from x 2575 to 2700 at the box's top edge is a zoning border crossing the top-row blocks x 2529-2618 and 2639-2726 (the blocks carry on above it to their tops near y 2140), not their top outline; their top is the box edge.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (AI), 2026-11-23: blocks chosen by eye on ruled close-ups; each corner then set on the outer edge of the block's thin line from the scan's dark-pixel runs (throwaway script), odd measurements checked by hand; checked on the labels picture"
